<title>NORWAY: Transocean Offshore completes merger.</title>
<headline>Transocean Offshore completes merger.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Houston-based Transocean Offshore Inc. said on Thursday it had acquired around 3.1 million shares in Transocean ASA bringing its total ownership in Transocean ASA to more than 99 percent.</p>
<p>The acquisition was in connection to the closing of Transocean Offshore's mandatory offer to Transocean ASA shareholders following the merger in September of Norway-based Transocean ASA and U.S. group Sonat Offshore Drilling Inc. to form Transocean Offshore Inc.</p>
<p>Transocean said it had paid $28.74 per share for the outstanding stake.</p>
<p>The company said that following the acquisition of the outstanding shares it intended to seek a delisting of Transocean ASA from the Oslo bourse.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
